## Timing Notes

The program uses the Raspberry Pi system timer for the displayed clock. The clock is not computed by counting loop iterations, so variations in loop runtime do not accumulate as clock drift.

The on-screen single-iteration loop timing can display `0 us`. This is expected because one polling-loop iteration can complete in less than the 1 microsecond resolution of the Raspberry Pi system timer.

During testing, the displayed clock advanced normally while the program continued accepting commands.

## Known Limitations

1. Sensor display is disabled in the clean terminal build.
2. The switch position table records switch positions commanded by this program; it is not independent physical switch feedback.
3. The terminal output avoids ANSI cursor-control sequences because `gtkterm` displayed those escape sequences as garbled characters.
4. Detailed automatic sensor timing collection is not fully implemented.
